<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Upper Aulaqi Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Nisab</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A sultanate of the Aulaqi tribes based at Nisab, one of the protected states in the hinterland of British Aden.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Aulaqi tribes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shabwa">Shabwa</a> region formed several states. The Upper Aulaqi Sultanate, based at Nisab, emerged as a distinct power by around 1800, alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/upper-aulaqi-sheikhdom">Upper Aulaqi Sheikhdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lower-aulaqi-sultanate">Lower Aulaqi Sultanate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans ruled a large but thinly populated territory of wadis and highland plateaus, where the Aulaqi were known as formidable fighters, many serving abroad as soldiers. The sultanate entered British protection by treaty and formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Aden Protectorate</a>. It joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a> in the 1960s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took power in 1967, the sultanate was abolished and incorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/upper-aulaqi-sultanate.jpg" alt="Upper Aulaqi Sultanate" width="320" height="203"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FederationOfSouthArabiaMap.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nisab</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Upper Awlaki Sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=upper-aulaqi-sultanate" aria-label="Upper Aulaqi Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5952 1638 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Upper Aulaqi Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6272 1894L6295 1853M6272 1894L6313 1863M6272 1894L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6272 1894h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6272 1894h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1884&amp;focus=upper-aulaqi-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
